# CRBS-39: Performance Testing Report

## 1. Objective

To evaluate the performance, reliability, and response time of the Conference Room Booking System under concurrent booking requests using k6.

## 2. Testing Environment

| Component | Specification |
|---|---|
| Operating System | Windows 11 |
| Laptop | Dell Vostro 3581 |
| Processor | Intel Core i3-7020U @ 2.30 GHz |
| CPU Cores | 2 |
| Logical Processors | 4 |
| RAM | 11.9 GB |
| Load Testing Tool | k6 v2.3.0 |
| Backend | Node.js / Express |
| Database | PostgreSQL |

## 3. Test Configuration

| Parameter | Configuration |
|---|---|
| Virtual Users | 5 maximum |
| Test Users | 5 dedicated test accounts |
| Conference Rooms | 5 dedicated test rooms |
| Target Bookings | 100 |
| Test Duration | 1 minute 59 seconds |
| Load Model | Constant Arrival Rate |
| Target Rate | 50 iterations per minute |
| Booking Endpoint | POST /api/bookings |

Each iteration logged in using a dedicated test account and attempted to create a booking for its assigned room.

## 4. Performance Test Results

| Metric | Observed Result |
|---|---:|
| Total Iterations | 100 |
| Successful Bookings | 100 |
| Failed Bookings | 0 |
| Booking Average Response Time | 67.07 ms |
| Booking Median Response Time | 65.26 ms |
| Booking p90 Response Time | 80.86 ms |
| Booking p95 Response Time | 94.35 ms |
| Maximum Booking Response Time | 130.44 ms |
| Booking Failure Rate | 0% |
| HTTP Request Failure Rate | 0% |
| Dropped Iterations | 0 |

## 5. Acceptance Criteria Evaluation

| Acceptance Criterion | Expected | Actual | Result |
|---|---|---|---|
| Concurrent users | 5 | 5 maximum VUs | Pass |
| Test rooms | 5 | 5 | Pass |
| Successful bookings | 100 | 100 | Pass |
| Duration | 2 minutes | 1m 59s | Pass |
| p95 response time | ≤ 3 seconds | 94.35 ms | Pass |
| Error rate | < 5% | 0% | Pass |

## 6. Observations

1. All 100 booking iterations completed successfully.
2. All booking requests returned HTTP 201.
3. No booking failures or HTTP request failures were observed.
4. The booking p95 response time was 94.35 ms, significantly below the 3-second threshold.
5. No iterations were dropped during the test.
6. The system handled the configured five virtual users without observed booking errors.

## 7. Conclusion

The Conference Room Booking System successfully passed the configured CRBS-39 performance test. All 100 booking iterations completed successfully with a 0% booking failure rate and a p95 booking response time of 94.35 ms.

The observed results satisfy all specified performance acceptance criteria under the tested configuration.

